 *
 * Runs on the Proxmox host via a systemd timer (see deploy/nxeon-nightly-scan.*),
 * gathers real read-only signals about the running system, and writes deduped
 * proposals into the `Improvement` table so the admin Improvements board
 * (app/admin/improvements) keeps filling up even when the owner's laptop is off.
 *
 * Every signal collector is wrapped in try/catch so a single failure (e.g. no
 * journal access) never aborts the whole run. Dedup: any proposal whose title
 * already exists in an active improvement (PROPOSED | APPROVED | IN_PROGRESS) is
 * skipped, so we never repropose the same finding night after night.
